# AWS VPC Gateway Endpoint POC for Private S3 Access

## Overview

This Proof of Concept (POC) demonstrates how to enable secure backup operations from a private subnet to Amazon S3 using VPC Gateway Endpoints, eliminating the need for NAT Gateway while maintaining strict security controls.

## Business Problem

The Engineering team identified a critical issue: removing the NAT Gateway from a private subnet would block all S3 communication, potentially hampering Business Continuity Planning (BCP) and Disaster Recovery (DR) processes. This POC solves this by implementing VPC Gateway Endpoints for S3 access without internet connectivity.

## Architecture

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                        VPC                                  │
│  ┌─────────────────┐                 ┌──────────────────┐   │
│  │  Public Subnet  │                 │  Private Subnet  │   │
│  │                 │                 │                  │   │
│  │  ┌───────────┐  │                 │  ┌────────────┐  │   │
│  │  │Bastion EC2│  │                 │  │Private EC2 │  │   │
│  │  │(Jump Host)│  │                 │  │            │  │   │
│  │  └───────────┘  │                 │  └────────────┘  │   │
│  └─────────────────┘                 └──────────────────┘   │
│                                              │               │
│                                              │               │
│                                    ┌─────────────────┐       │
│                                    │ VPC Gateway     │       │
│                                    │ Endpoint (S3)   │       │
│                                    └─────────────────┘       │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
                                              │
